{
  "statement": "D.59",
  "purpose": "Every local Fermat point for ell=3,5 has exactly one nonunit coordinate",
  "general_exponent_proof": "ell^r and ell are congruent modulo ell(ell-1); this is the exponent of (Z/ell^2)^*.",
  "general_radius_proof": "rho=(r+1/(ell-1))/ell^r<1: it holds at r=1, and multiplying the right side by ell increases its excess.",
